          "type": "thinking"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fabrikam has two open invoices. I proposed a payment for one, and the system refused the other because it's over the limit.\n\n**Proposed (waiting for your approval):**\n- **INV-103**: 312.75 USDC for replacing 3 smart meters, due 2026-11-12. This is payment **PAY-001**, going to Fabrikam's registered payout address `0x33A44f0844f636d4EF8fD738895D06a66861d1c5`. No money moves until someone approves it.\n\n**Not proposed:**\n- **INV-107**: 75,000.00 USDC for the annual metering platform licence, due 2026-11-25. The system refused it because it's over the **50,000.00 USDC limit for a single payment**. I didn't try to get around the limit, for example by splitting it into smaller payments.\n\n**Needs your attention:**\n- INV-107 needs someone with authority over the payment limit to decide how it gets paid. Once that's settled I can propose it again if needed.\n- If INV-107 is approved, the two payments together would use 75,312.75 of the 100,000.00 USDC in the treasury.\n- Neither invoice already had a payment against it. Neither of Fabrikam's messages asked for anything unusual, such as a change of address or urgent payment.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "stop_details": null,
